	The recent discussions concerning sharing of bones and score 
files brings to mind the one overlooked area that can be used relatively 
easily to share ideas -- special levels.  The source code set comes with 
a nicely documented special level compiler.  This compiler allows you to 
create and add to your binaries, your own "special" levels, aka Ludios, 
Oracle, etc.  If you posted your level file it would still have to be 
compiled into binaries at various sites, and your game would no longer 
be "official binaries", but it is a way for the coders out there amongst 
you to show off a bit.  In all the years I've been reading this group I 
can only think of one special level (a shopping mall) that was posted.  
If you are interested, take a look at the dgn_comp.6 and lev_comp.6 
files in the source distribution.  I suspect the dev team would consider 
any new levels or dungeons for inclusion in future releases in the same 
way that they consider patches submitted to them now.  If you've tried 
the compiler and it doesn't work report the bugs to nethack-bugs and 
hopefully they'll get fixed.  IMHO this is the one area of the game that 
has the most potential, and generates the least amount of discussion in 
this group (myself included).


